> # Empty map
> HEIGHT 5 5
Cell [0.000, 0.000] size 64.000 m, depth 0, 0 returns
  No data (unknown cell)
  nodes visited: 1
> NEAREST 1 1
No obstacles in the map
  nodes visited: 1
> RANGE 0 0 64 64
0 returns in range, 0 obstacle returns
  nodes visited: 1
> COLLIDE 0 0 64 64
CLEAR - region is free
  nodes visited: 1
> OBJECTS
No moving objects
> DELETE 1 1
No return at (1.00, 1.00)
> MOVE 3 1 1
No object with id 3
> REMOVEOBJ 3
No object with id 3
> # Invalid input must never crash
> INSERT abc 1 1
Error: 'abc' is not a valid number
> INSERT 1 2
Usage: INSERT x y z [id]
> INSERT 100 100 1
Rejected: (100.00, 100.00) is outside the map. Map: [0.00, 64.00] x [0.00, 64.00] m, ground z = 0.00 m
> INSERT -0.5 5 1
Rejected: (-0.50, 5.00) is outside the map. Map: [0.00, 64.00] x [0.00, 64.00] m, ground z = 0.00 m
> INSERT 0 0 nan
Error: 'nan' is not a valid number
> INSERT 1 1 1 -5
Error: id must be >= 0
> INSERT 1 1 1 2.5
Error: '2.5' is not a valid integer
> INIT 0 0 -4
Error: size must be positive
> INIT 0 0 0
Error: size must be positive
> MAP 0 5
Error: cols and rows must be in 1 .. 200
> DEPTH 5
Usage: DEPTH [cols rows]
> FOO
Unknown command 'FOO' (type HELP)
> REMOVEOBJ 0
Error: id must be > 0 (id 0 is the static scene)
> MOVE 0 1 1
Error: only moving objects (id > 0) can be moved
> LOAD does_not_exist.txt
Error: cannot open 'does_not_exist.txt'
> HEIGHT 70 70
(70.00, 70.00) is outside the map
> # Boundary points (closed interval) are accepted
> INSERT 0 0 0
Inserted (0.00, 0.00, 0.00) id=0
> INSERT 64 64 0
Inserted (64.00, 64.00, 0.00) id=0
